{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.MarkovPairZ2","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovPairZ2","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceProduct"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.markov_pair_z2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.markov_pair_z2","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovPairZ2.lean#L62-L80","doc":"**All-pairs Markov-trace identity (depth-2 cap).**\n\nFor an adjacent pair of \"trivial\" generator chains (each chain\nis `σ_i · 1 + 0`, i.e. the bare braid generator at index `i`),\neach `vertexVolume` equals `z`, so the pair's trace is `z²`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:markov-pair-z2","label":"prop:markov-pair-z2","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-pair-z2.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.markov_pair_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.markov_pair_value","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovPairZ2.lean#L45-L60","doc":"The Markov-trace value of an adjacent pair `[c₁, c₂]`,\nconditional on a `MarkovTraceAxioms z` instance.  Two cons-axiom\napplications give\n\n  `trace [c₁, c₂] = vertexVolume z c₁ · vertexVolume z c₂`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}